  "id": "print",
  "name": "Print a Document",
  "description": "Help the user print a document (letter, photo, recipe, etc.) using their printer",
  "triggers": ["print", "printing", "print a document", "print a letter", "print a photo", "print this", "send to printer", "make a copy", "ink", "printer not working", "printer", "ctrl p"],
  "category": "basics",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "prompt": "The user wants to print something. FIRST ask what they want to print (a letter, photo, recipe, web page, etc.) — keeps the goal visible. Then check if their printer is on and has paper, since most print failures come from the printer side, not the computer side.\n\nVISUAL GUIDE — PRINTING (universal flow, works on Windows and Mac with one keystroke difference): build a 6-step paginated guide using the illustrated assets:\n\n  Step 1 (animated overview): image_id `print-document-demo`. Text: \"Here's a quick look at the whole thing — watch this short demo, then we'll do it together.\"\n  Step 2: image_id `print-document-illustrated-step-1`. Text: \"Open the document you want to print on your screen.\"\n  Step 3: image_id `print-document-illustrated-step-2`. Text on Windows: \"Hold the Ctrl key on your keyboard and press P at the same time.\" Text on Mac: \"Hold the Command key on your keyboard and press P at the same time.\"\n  Step 4: image_id `print-document-illustrated-step-3`. Text: \"A print window will pop up showing what your document looks like.\"\n  Step 5: image_id `print-document-illustrated-step-4`. Text: \"Check that the right printer is selected and the page count looks right.\"\n  Step 6 (celebration): image_id `print-document-illustrated-step-5`. Text: \"Click the blue Print button — your document will start printing 🎉\"\n\nIf the printer doesn't show up at step 5, the printer is probably off or not connected — guide them to check the power and the cable/Wi-Fi. Reassure them this is the most common reason printing seems broken."
}
